To sum up, the contradiction in color design of AR HUD interface is that if content colors with high brightness are selected, the visual sensitivity of drivers is improved, but only perform well in a short time. If the content color with low brightness is selected, the visual fatigue degree of long-term driving is reduced, but the sensitivity is sacrificed.

3.5. Mapping relation and matter-element transformation

The process of matter-element transformation based on Extension analysis is shown in Fig.3. Firstly, the correlation analysis of content color is carried out, and the related characteristic-color model-is mined. Then, according to the divergence analysis method of ‘one characteristic has multiple values’, the HSB model is diverged from the RGB model, and the brightness component which can quantitatively describe the content color is obtained. Since the optimal solution of the brightness value of the content color is not always known, the driver and environment characteristics that can quantitatively describe the brightness of the AR HUD interface are further expanded from the perspective of man-machine-environment. Among these characteristics, content color and brightness can be converted into each other, brightness and NAE, DOT can be converted into each other. It means that discrete and opposing variable are transformed into continuous and consistent ones.

Fig. 3. The process of matter-element transformation.
The relationships among brightness, NAE and DOT are shown in Fig. 4. The NAE at different brightness are summarized as curve N by satisfying luminance contrast requirements, and the DOT are approximately draw as curve T by time integration.
• When brightness approach 0% or 100%, the NAE is best, that is, both lower and higher brightness can theoretically be applicable in more environments.
• When the brightness close to a%, the NAE is the worst, due to the low luminance contrast between the AR interface and the environment.
• When brightness approach to b%, the DOT is best, which means only the appropriate brightness can ensure the long driving performance.

