Now, the dilemma problem in AR HUD interface design has been transformed into finding a proper brightness that balance the NAE and DOT, so that the driver comprehensive visual performance to achieve the best. In the next section, we will establish the color selection model, helping engineers and designers to design graphics or character colors more scientifically and systematically. 4. Color selection models for AR HUD interface
For the optimal solution of content color, the distance function from the selected matter-element to optimal value is constructed in this chapter.
In Fig. 5, the given standard positive fields of NAE and DOT are N0 and T0 respectively (N0 and T0 are determined by the engineering). The positive field of the brightness is X = 〈0%, 100%〉, where the expected interval that meet the requirements of NAE and DOT is X0 = 〈p0, q0〉 and x is the selected brightness value.
When the optimal value of brightness has been given, it is only required to verify whether x is within the interval X0 and how relevant is it to the best value. The calculation model based on the brightness is established in the first section of this chapter. If the optimal value is uncertain, the x needs to be evaluated by NAE and DOT. The calculation model based on the NAE and DOT is established in the second section of this chapter.
