In the AR HUD interface design, the color should be selected according to the attributes of content information,
such as viewing time, priority, state variation, etc. For example, the content with low priority and long viewing time
can choose content color with lower brightness. And for content with high priority and short viewing time, a content
color with higher brightness can be selected. Consequently, different weights can be assigned to the indicators affecting color selection to build a weighted color selection model. In this section, we define the weight of NAE (K(n)) as w% , and the weight of DOT (K(t)) as 1 − w%. The preliminary model can be optimized as formula (32). Similarly, the closer the value of K'(x) is to 0, the smaller distance from the selected value x to the optimal solution.

