5. Conclusions

The AR HUD will provide advanced information on security and entertainment in intelligent vehicles in the near future. By visualizing lanes, cars, pedestrians, and predicting the expected path of cars, it can build public trust in autonomous driving. Based on the matter element analysis and dependent function, the paper transforms the discrete problem into continuous one, and provides a solution about the content color selection in AR HUD interface design. The mapping relationship between the content color and brightness of AR HUD is analyzed qualitatively, and a quantitative weighted color selection model is established to reflect the tendency towards selected elements to the optimal interval by constructing dependent functions. Finally, a simple evaluation method and an application case are given.
In future studies, we will conduct series human factors experiments by driving simulators, and collect more engineering data to conduct a more accurate and specific quantitative analysis of the relationship between brightness and DOT and NML. Through continuous modification of matter-element relationship, change curve, optimal interval and weight value, the final calculation result is more scientific and reasonable, and provides effective support for the optimization of AR HUD interface design in intelligent vehicle.

